# Cross-origin isolation is a hard launch constraint — see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
# Without both headers the page is not cross-origin-isolated and the
# SharedArrayBuffer agent overlay falls back to the slower copy path.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
# Content-Security-Policy, directives derived from code, not guesswork:
# - script 'self' only (Vite emits no inline scripts in production builds)
# - 'wasm-unsafe-eval' for the wasm-bindgen decision layer (instantiateStreaming)
# - style 'unsafe-inline' for React's inline style attributes
# - img data: for basemaps embedded as base64, blob: for report/object URLs
# - connect: api.open-meteo.com for the weather panel; restapi.amap.com for the
#   POI lookup. Both are user-triggered and both need a key the user supplies.
# - Amap is optional: webapi.amap.com is only contacted when a key is set, and
#   without one the map step falls back to typed coordinates.
#
# - UNVERIFIED: the two hosts above are the ones this codebase names in its own
#   source. The JS SDK also pulls map tiles at runtime, from hosts we have not
#   enumerated because that needs a live key to observe. A deployment that
#   enables the base map must check the console for CSP violations once and add
#   whatever tile host appears; the map step degrades to coordinates either
#   way, so a miss here breaks the picture and not the flow.
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://webapi.amap.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://webapi.amap.com; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://api.open-meteo.com https://restapi.amap.com; worker-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'
